{{Quote|Ah! I see you still have your lightsaber.''"<br />"Ezra's ''lightsaber.''"<br />"''True, he constructed it and by all accounts it served him well. Then he passed it onto you. You have since made your own modifications, so it is now ''your'' lightsaber''.|Huyang and Sabine Wren|<ref name="Part Two">{{Ahsoka|Part Two: Toil and Trouble}}</ref>}}
'''Sabine Wren's lightsaber''', formerly '''Ezra Bridger's second lightsaber''', was a [[Color|green]]-bladed [[lightsaber]] constructed by [[Ezra Bridger]], a [[Padawan]] and [[Spectres|rebel]] prior to the [[Battle of Yavin]], sometime after his [[Ezra Bridger's first lightsaber|original lightsaber]] was destroyed by the [[Sith Lord]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] during the [[Mission to Malachor|mission]] to [[Malachor]].

Before his disappearance with [[Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn]] aboard the ''[[Chimaera]]'', Bridger gave his lightsaber to [[Mandalorian]] [[Soldier|warrior]] [[Sabine Wren]], who kept and modified it during and after her [[Jedi training|training]] from [[Ahsoka Tano]] in the years after Bridger disappeared into [[hyperspace]] with the [[Admiral]].

==Specifications==
[[File:EzraBridger2ndLightsaber-TLC.png|thumb|left|250px|Ezra's second lightsaber emitted a green blade.]]
[[Sabine Wren]]'s [[lightsaber]]<ref name="Name">{{SW|url=news/sdcc-2023-ahsoka-props|text=SDCC 2023: See ''Ahsoka'' Props and Costumes from the Lucasfilm Pavilion}}</ref> featured a hilt with a [[Color|black]] grip and silver accents.<ref name="DB" /> It originally belonged to the [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Ezra Bridger]], who passed the blade along to Wren after it had served him well.<ref name="Part Two" /> It was also built to the more traditional lightsaber design,<ref name="Steps Into Shadow" /> as opposed to his [[Ezra Bridger's first lightsaber|old]] [[lightsaber-blaster hybrid]].<ref name="Visual Guide">''[[Star Wars Rebels: The Visual Guide]]''</ref>

In Wren's possession, the hilt's overall design remained mostly unchanged, albeit with some modifications, including a larger emitter shroud.<ref name="Part Two" /> The guard pieces she installed by the blade emitter served to protect her hands from it.<ref name="DB Sabine">{{Databank|sabine-s-lightsaber|Sabine's lightsaber}}</ref>

==History==
{{Quote|Here. Do your thing.''"<br />"''What thing?''"<br />"''Your lightsaber, take it.''"<br />"''You keep it.''"<br />"''What? ''"<br />"''I don’t need it. Besides, you’ve been training.''"<br />"''Very funny.''"<br />"''No, I’m serious.''"<br />"''<nowiki />''Take'' it.''"<br />"''I gave it to you, it’s yours now.|Ezra and Sabine Wren, when Sabine tries to return the lightsaber to its original owner|<ref name="Part Seven">{{Ahsoka|Part Seven: Dreams and Madness}}</ref>}}
[[File:EzraSecondLightsaber-DB.jpg|thumb|right|300px|Ezra wielding the lightsaber in combat.]]
Following the [[Mission to Malachor#Showdown with Darth Vader|destruction]] of Ezra Bridger's lightsaber by the [[Sith Lord]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] on [[Malachor]], Bridger built a new lightsaber<ref name="DB" /> sometime between [[3 BBY]]<ref name="Twilight of the Apprentice Date" /> and [[2 BBY]]<ref name="Date note" /> During the [[Skirmish on Krownest|mission]] to [[Krownest]], Sabine Wren wielded the lightsaber when she [[Lightsaber combat|fought]] [[Governor]] [[Gar Saxon]] who wielded the [[Darksaber]].<ref name="Legacy of Mandalore">{{Rebels|Legacy of Mandalore}}</ref>

Later on, during a mission to [[Mission to Faos Station|investigate]] what the [[Galactic Empire]] was doing with large kyber crystals, [[Saw Gerrera]] used the weapon to ignite one of such crystals to destroy the Imperial [[freighter]] that was carrying it.<ref name="In the Name of the Rebellion">{{Rebels|In the Name of the Rebellion}}</ref>

During the [[Liberation of Lothal]], after Bridger's strike team seized control of the [[Imperial Complex (Lothal)|Imperial Complex]], Bridger left his lightsaber in the hands of Wren after [[Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn]] issued an ultimatum in which Bridger had to turn himself in alone onboard the ''[[Chimaera]]'' to prevent [[Capital City]] from being [[Orbital bombardment|bombarded]]. After Bridger managed to repel Thrawn's [[Imperial Navy|Imperial fleet]] from [[Lothal]], Wren used the lightsaber to break through a window and out of the Complex as the rebels [[Self-destruct mechanism|rigged the building to explode]], providing them with a quick escape route.<ref name="FRAF" />

[[File:SabineWrensLightsaber-CGSWG.png|thumb|left|200px|Sabine Wren, as the apprentice of Ahsoka Tano, wields the lightsaber as her own.]]
Since possessing the lightsaber, Wren added her own modifications to it, though she insisted the lightsaber still belonged to Bridger. Despite its creator, [[Huyang]] noted that her own additions therefore made her the owner rather than the former.<ref name="Part Two" /> Wren used the saber to duel [[Shin Hati]] outside the [[LothalNet comm tower E-272|comm tower]] on [[Lothal]]<ref name="Part One" /> and later [[Seatos]].<ref name="Part Four">{{Ahsoka|Part Four: Fallen Jedi}}</ref> Wren believed [[Ahsoka Tano]] to be dead and accepted the offer of [[Baylan Skoll]] to travel with them to the [[Far galaxy|other galaxy]], with the saber being confiscated.<ref name="Part Four" /> After arriving on [[Peridea]] in the other galaxy and meet [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn]], he agreed to let Wren search for Ezra, they returned the saber which Wren used to defend herself of [[Bandits of Peridea|bandits]].<ref name="Part Six">{{Ahsoka|Part Six: Far, Far Away}}</ref>

After finally finding Bridger, they were attacked by Hati and bandits. Wren attempted to return the saber to him, but Bridger shared the same viewpoint as Huyang, telling Wren that she should keep it. Although she opposed his stance on the matter, Bridger urged Wren to keep the lightsaber as it belonged to her. She used it to fight the bandits and Hati.<ref name="Part Seven">{{Ahsoka|Part Seven: Dreams and Madness}}</ref> Bridger later built a [[Ezra's third lightsaber|new one]] with a blue kyber crystal. In their attempt to stop Thrawn's return to the [[The galaxy|known galaxy]], Wren used her saber to dispatch [[Night Trooper]]s and a [[Zombie|zombified]] [[Death trooper|Death Trooper]].<ref name="Part Eight">{{Ahsoka|Part Eight: The Jedi, the Witch, and the Warlord}}</ref>

{{Weapon-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Ezra Bridger's second lightsaber was first revealed in the tenth episode of the ''[[The Star Wars Show]]'', a series of behind-the-scenes [[Wikipedia:YouTube|YouTube]] videos produced by [[StarWars.com]] that give official news regarding upcoming ''Star Wars'' media and events.<ref name="Episode 10">{{StarWarsShow|Qe3LSQiMJUk|Star Wars Rebels Season 3 Clip, Gareth Edwards Interview, and More!|sw_url=video/the-star-wars-show-episode-10}}</ref> It made its first appearance on the animated television series ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]'' in the [[Star Wars Rebels Season Three|third season]] premiere episode ''[[Star Wars Rebels: Steps Into Shadow]]''.<ref name="Steps Into Shadow" />

